//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Package
// $Module name: BrittishHolidays.pkg
// $Author     : Peter Crook, Ancilla Software
// Created     : 17/ 2/2001
//
// Description : Function that returns the name of UK notable dates from a date variable.
//
// Caveat      : All dates are subject to change and regional and institutional variations.
//               Up-to-date details of bank holidays can be found at:
//               http://www.direct.gov.uk/en/Governmentcitizensandrights/LivingintheUK/DG_073741
//               There is a lot of information about holidays in various countries (as well as
//               other calendar stuff) at TimeAndDate.com
//
// Note        : To create a similar package for another country, copy the function below and
//               simply change the name and wordings and possibly also what should constitute the holidays
//               for your country. All the underlying holiday functions can be found in oCalendarHolidays.pkg
//               The HolidayName function is used by the Holidays.vw sample view; the oCreateDates_bp business process.
//
// $Rev History:
//    2011-02-03 BritishHolidays.pkg Module header created
//    2011-02-10 Revised and renamed by PDC, Ancilla Software.
//               The ByRef variable has been changed to an integer with the following significance:
//               1  Bank holiday in England and Wales
//               2  Bank holiday in Scotland
//               4  Bank holiday in Northern Ireland
//               Combinations of the above might be returned (e.g. 3 for date that is a bank holiday in only England, Wales and Scotland).
//               Thus the returned value will be 'True' if the date is a bank holiday anywhere in the UK.
//
//    2025-01-23 Revised and moved all helper functions to the common oCalendarHolidays.pkg. (NS)
//
//****************************************************************************
//
Use cNationalHolidays.pkg

// The regions of the UK bank holidays (2026-11-21). They are the bits HolidayDetails gives in iRegions, and the
// values for ghoCalendarHolidays' piHolidayRegion, which tells the working-day functions (IsWorkingDay,
// AddWorkingDays, WorkingDaysBetween) whose bank holidays are days off:
//     Set piHolidayRegion of ghoCalendarHolidays to CI_UKRegionScotland
// 0, the default, is England and Wales. A bank holiday of the whole UK is a day off in every region.
Define CI_UKRegionEnglandWales    for 1
Define CI_UKRegionScotland        for 2
Define CI_UKRegionNorthernIreland for 4
Define CI_UKRegionAny             for 7   // a bank holiday in any part of the UK is a day off
Define CI_UKBankHolidayAllRegions for 8   // the bit HolidayDetails gives a bank holiday of the whole UK

Object oBrittishHolidays is a cNationalHolidays

    // A 2-character ISO_Short string, according to the list:
    // https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#search/code/
    Set psISO_Short to "GB"
    Set psLocaleName to "en-GB"    // the month and day names in the country's language
    Set pbRegionBits to True       // the days' official value is the bank holiday's regions (HolidayDetails' iRegions)

    // THE DAYS (2026-11-26): looked up in this order - the first that falls on a date names it. AddDay gives a day by
    // one of the library's date functions (oCalendarHolidays.pkg), AddFixedDay by its month and day; the last argument
    // is the bank holiday's regions - the CI_UKRegion... bits, 8 (CI_UKBankHolidayAllRegions) for the whole UK, 0 for
    // a day that is not a bank holiday. HolidayName and IsDateAHoliday both read this list (cNationalHolidays.pkg).

    // *** Holidays that occur in only one year ***
    Send AddFixedDay 4 29 "Royal Wedding (UK)" 8
    Send SetDayYears 2011 2011
    Send AddFixedDay 6 5 "Queen's Diamond Jubilee (UK)" 8
    Send SetDayYears 2012 2012
    Send AddFixedDay 6 3 "Platinum Jubilee Bank Holiday (UK)" 8
    Send SetDayYears 2022 2022
    Send AddFixedDay 9 19 "State Funeral of Queen Elizabeth II (UK)" 8
    Send SetDayYears 2022 2022
    Send AddFixedDay 5 8 "Coronation of King Charles III (UK)" 8
    Send SetDayYears 2023 2023

    // *** Bank holidays ***

    // A day and its bank holiday: the day is "(UK)" - a bank holiday - when the bank holiday falls on it;
    // when the day is a Saturday or Sunday, the bank holiday is the next Monday (or Tuesday) instead.
    // New Year's Day - 1st January.
    Send AddDay "NewYearsDay" "New Year's Day (UK)" 8
    Send SetDayAlsoOn "NewYearsDayBH"
    Send AddDay "NewYearsDay" "New Year's Day" 0
    Send AddDay "NewYearsDayBH" "New Year's Holiday (UK)" 8

    // The Scots get an extra day at New Year on 2nd January - or the next Monday or Tuesday.
    Send AddDay "ScotishNewYearHoliday" "New Year's Holiday (Scotland)" 2

    // St. Patrick's Day (Northern Ireland) - 17th March.
    Send AddDay "SaintPatricksDay" "St. Patrick's Day (NI)" 4
    Send SetDayAlsoOn "StPatricksDayBH"
    Send AddDay "SaintPatricksDay" "St. Patrick's Day" 0
    Send AddDay "StPatricksDayBH" "St. Patrick's Day Holiday (NI)" 4

    // Easter Monday - not a bank holiday in Scotland.
    Send AddDay "EasterMonday" "Easter Monday (not Scotland)" 5

    // Early May Bank Holiday - 1st Monday in May.
    Send AddDay "EarlyMayBH" "Early May Bank Holiday (UK)" 8

    // Spring Bank Holiday - last Monday in May.
    Send AddDay "MemorialDay" "Spring Bank Holiday (UK)" 8

    // Summer Bank Holiday - 1st Monday in August in Scotland, last Monday in England, Wales and Northern Ireland.
    Send AddDay "SummerBHScot" "Summer Bank Holiday (Scotland)" 2
    Send AddDay "SummerBHEngNI" "Summer Bank Holiday (England, Wales and NI)" 5

    // Battle of the Boyne Day (Northern Ireland) - 12th July.
    Send AddDay "BattleOfTheBoyne" "Battle of the Boyne (NI)" 4
    Send SetDayAlsoOn "BattleOfTheBoyneBH"
    Send AddDay "BattleOfTheBoyne" "Battle of the Boyne" 0
    Send AddDay "BattleOfTheBoyneBH" "Battle of the Boyne (NI)" 4

    // St. Andrew's Day (Scotland) - 30th November.
    Send AddDay "StAndrewsDay" "St. Andrew's Day (Scotland)" 2
    Send SetDayAlsoOn "StAndrewsDayBH"
    Send AddDay "StAndrewsDay" "St. Andrew's Day" 0
    Send AddDay "StAndrewsDayBH" "St. Andrew's Day (Scotland)" 2

    // Christmas Day - 25th December.
    Send AddDay "ChristmasDay" "Christmas Day (UK)" 8
    Send SetDayAlsoOn "ChristmasDayBH"
    Send AddDay "ChristmasDay" "Christmas Day" 0
    Send AddDay "ChristmasDayBH" "Christmas Day Holiday (UK)" 8

    // Boxing Day - 26th December.
    Send AddDay "SecondDayChristmas" "Boxing Day (UK)" 8
    Send SetDayAlsoOn "BoxingDayBH"
    Send AddDay "SecondDayChristmas" "Boxing Day" 0
    Send AddDay "BoxingDayBH" "Boxing Day Holiday (UK)" 8

    // *** Other notable dates ***
    Send AddDay "NewYearsEve" "New Year's Eve" 0
    Send AddDay "NewYearsDay" "New Year's Day" 0

    // Twelfth Night - 5th January (take your decorations down today!)
    //
    Send AddDay "Epiphany" "Twelfth Night" 0
    Send SetDayOffset -1 0

    // Valentines Day - 14th February
    //
    Send AddDay "ValentinesDay" "Valentine's Day" 0

    // Burns Night, when the Scots celebrate the birth in 1759 of their 'National Poet' Robert Burns.
    // Note for pendants: it does seem to be Burns Night (no possessive) even though it's celebrating
    // Robert Burns's birth.
    //
    Send AddFixedDay 1 25 "Burns Night" 0

    // St. David's Day, celebrated in Wales - 1st March
    //
    Send AddFixedDay 3 1 "St. David's Day" 0

    // Start of European (British) Summer Time - last Sunday in March (at 1am)
    //
    Send AddDay "EUSummerTimeStart" "British Summer Time starts" 0

    // St.George's Day, not widely celebrated in England - 23rd April
    //
    Send AddFixedDay 4 23 "St. George's Day" 0

    // Easter Day - the first Sunday on or after the first full moon after the vernal equinox.
    //
    Send AddDay "EasterDay" "Easter Day" 0
    Send AddDay "FeastOfChristTheKing" "Feast of Christ the King" 0

    // End of European (British) Summer Time - last Sunday in October (at 1am)
    //
    Send AddDay "EUSummerTimeEnd" "British Summer Time ends" 0

    // Halloween - 31st October (watch out for the witches!)
    //
    Send AddDay "Halloween" "Halloween" 0

    // Remembrance Sunday - the first Sunday after Remmebrance Day, 11th November
    Send AddDay "RemembranceSunday" "Remembrance Sunday" 0

    // *** Movable holidays ***
    // Dates that depend on the date of Easter Day.
    Send AddDay "Advent1" "Advent Sunday" 0
    Send AddDay "Advent2" "2nd Advent Sunday" 0
    Send AddDay "Advent3" "3d Advent Sunday" 0

    // This needs to be after ChristMasEve because it can fall on the same day,
    // and we then wants to return Christmas Eve instead.
    Send AddDay "Advent4" "4th Advent Sunday" 0
    Send AddDay "AshWednesday" "Ash Wednesday" 0

    // Shrove Tuesday, Pancake Day - the day before Ash Wednesday
    //
    Send AddDay "AshWednesday" "Shrove Tuesday (Pancake Day)" 0
    Send SetDayOffset -1 0
    Send AddDay "GoodFriday" "Good Friday (UK)" 8
    Send AddDay "AprilFoolsDay" "April Fools' Day" 0
    Send AddDay "Thanksgiving" "Thanksgiving Day" 0
    Send AddDay "PalmSunday" "Palm Sunday" 0
    Send AddDay "AscensionDay" "Ascension Day" 0
    Send AddDay "WhitSunday" "Whit Sunday" 0
    Send AddDay "WhitMonday" "Whit Monday" 0
    Send AddDay "AllSaintsDay" "All Saints Day" 0
    Send AddDay "NationalDay" "National Day" 1
    Send AddFixedDay 3 1 "St David's Day (Wales)" 0  // 1 of March.
    Send AddFixedDay 3 17 "St Patrick's Day (Northern Ireland)" 0  // 17 of March.
    Send AddFixedDay 4 23 "St George's Day (England)" 0  // 23 of April.
    Send AddFixedDay 11 30 "St Andrew's Day (Skottland)" 0  // 30 of November.

    // Spring Equinox
    Send AddDay "VernalEquinox" "Spring Equinox" 0

    // Autumn Equinox
    Send AddDay "AutumnalEquinox" "Autumn Equinox" 0

    // This day needs to be _after_ the WhitSunday.
    // So when WhitSunday falls on the last Sunday in May,
    // only the WhitSunday will get generated. Else the
    // Mother's Day would show up at that day.
    Send AddDay "MothersDay" "Mothers' Day" 0
    Send AddDay "FathersDay" "Fathers' Day" 0


    // Is the date a bank holiday - a day off by law - in the region? Asked by the working-day functions of
    // cCalendarHolidays (IsWorkingDay), with its piHolidayRegion: one or more CI_UKRegion* bits, 0 for England and
    // Wales. A bank holiday of the whole UK is a day off in every region.
    Function IsOfficialDayOff Date dDate Integer iRegion Returns Boolean
        tHoliday Holiday

        If (iRegion = 0) Begin
            Move CI_UKRegionEnglandWales to iRegion
        End
        Get HolidayDetails dDate to Holiday
        If ((Holiday.iRegions iand CI_UKBankHolidayAllRegions) <> 0) Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        Function_Return ((Holiday.iRegions iand iRegion) <> 0)
    End_Function

End_Object
